1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,854
When your fingers wrinkle in the bath,
it isn't just your skin soaking up water.

2
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:09,205
Instead, your nerves tell the blood
vessels under the skin to tighten,

3
00:00:09,205 --> 00:00:12,507
so the fingertip shrinks and
its skin buckles into folds.

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,304
And that's why a finger with a
damaged nerve doesn't wrinkle,

5
00:00:16,304 --> 00:00:18,890
which doctors have even
used as a nerve test.

6
00:00:19,183 --> 00:00:21,255
So the wrinkles might be on purpose,

7
00:00:21,255 --> 00:00:23,787
working like tire treads
to grip wet things,

8
00:00:23,787 --> 00:00:26,262
although scientists
still argue about that.

9
00:00:26,567 --> 00:00:29,978
And the folds even come back
in the same pattern every time,

10
00:00:29,978 --> 00:00:33,390
because the blood vessels
underneath stay in the same place.
